  static_cast<std::string>(orderBy), order_by_string's "ORDER BY",
  before its terms; statement_serializer's dynamic specialization
  (then 2272-2279) passed it on, while the static (2265) and multi
  (2290) forms added the keyword themselves.
- Options offered: (a) widen the Purpose to name both, a variant; (b) a
  refactor moving the keyword to statement_serializer, as the other two
  forms have it. Claude's lean (b), on this line rather than a pull
  request off dev (trueqbit: one working and review line); trueqbit:
  "your leans", and "throw away the order_by_string base tag and
  directly stream "ORDER BY"".
- Call sites checked: serialize_order_by takes a dynamic order-by only
  from statement_serializer's dynamic specialization, which now adds
  the keyword; streaming.h:249 passes the static terms of a multi
  ORDER BY; no other code converts an order-by node to std::string.
- Pinned by the serializer tests: tests/statement_serializer_tests/
  ast/dynamic_order_by.cpp (full "ORDER BY ..." through serialize()),
  conditions.cpp, column_names.cpp. Not compiled; trueqbit and CI build.

